  <page_number>201</page_number>
  <running_head>CANTICVM / CORVM.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>Cc. 3</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Sed tamen venustula,</l>
    <l n="2">Hinc velut mapalibus</l>
    <l n="3">Quæ tetendit Æthiops</l>
    <l n="4">Educata fordidis:</l>
    <l n="5">Inde talis qualia</l>
    <l n="6">Sollomonis fulgida</l>
    <l n="7">Cernimus tentoria.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">6. Ergo ne me, virgines,</l>
    <l n="9">Ceu nigellam, spernite,</l>
    <l n="10">Decolorem torridi</l>
    <l n="11">Solis æstu reddidam:</l>
    <l n="12">Dum misella, fratribus,</l>
    <l n="13">Vna communis quibus</l>
    <l n="14">Contigit parens mihi,</l>
    <l n="15">Me foras pellentibus,</l>
    <l n="16">Exteras ad vineas,</l>
    <l n="17">Exulo procul meam</l>
    <l n="18">Tristis extra vincam.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">7. At meum corculum,</l>
    <l n="20">Expetenti te mihi,</l>
    <l n="21">Quæso te, renuntia,</l>
    <l n="22">Gregem vbi pascas tuum.</l>
    <l n="23">Grata vbi tuo gregi.</l>
    <l n="24">Solis æstu feruidi</l>
    <l n="25">Præbeas vmbracula.</l>
    <l n="26">Næque ad istorum greges,</l>
    <l n="27">Qui sodales se tuos</l>
    <l n="28">Impudenter iactitant,</l>
    <l n="29">Ceu latebras quæritans,</l>
    <l n="30">Cur ego confedero?</l>
    <l n="31" type="heading" level="3" para="true">SPONSVS.</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">8. Tène vero nesciam</l>
    <l n="33">Hoc rogare dixerim,</l>
    <l n="34">Virginum pulcherrima?</l>
    <l n="35">Qua meus gregex, defpice.</l>
    <l n="36">Prata tundens florea.</l>
    <l n="37">Fixerit vestigia.</l>
    <l n="38">Hic gregis pastoribus</l>
    <l n="39">Iunge temet proximam:</l>
    <l n="40">Tu capellas hic tuas</l>
    <l n="41">Coge cunctas sedula.</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">9. Cæterùm, dicaculi</l>
    <l n="43">Quicquid isti iactitent.</l>
    <l n="44">Totius te corporis</l>
    <l n="45">Tam graui, tam regia</l>
    <l n="46">Dignitate præditam,</l>
    <l n="47">Comparo Memphiticis</l>
    <l n="48">Cum meis iugalibus.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">10. O genarum fulgidis</l>
    <l n="50">Hinc &amp; hinc inauribus</l>
    <l n="51">Temperatam purpuram!</l>
    <l n="52">O nouum colli decus,</l>
    <l n="53">Torque cincti gemmeo!</l>
    <l n="54" para="true">11. Istud &amp; tamen decus</l>
    <l n="55">Ecce me iuuat nouis</l>
    <l n="56">Auditare honoribus:</l>
    <l n="57">Sparsi mox argenteis</l>
    <l n="58">Clauulis monilia</l>
    <l n="59">Additurus aurea,</l>
    <l n="60" type="heading" level="2" para="true">SPONSA.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">12. Euge, Rex gregalibus</l>
    <l n="62">Cinctus accubat suis,</l>
    <l n="63">Sponsa cuius ad latus</l>
    <l n="64">Ter beata confidens,</l>
    <l n="65">Tota nardi diffluo</l>
    <l n="66">Suaue olentis vnguin^a.</l>
    <l n="67" para="true">13. Ille verò molliter</l>
    <l n="68">Se sinu condens meo,</l>
    <l n="69">Charus vnicè mihi,</l>
    <l n="70">Affidentem recreat,</l>
    <l n="71">Fascis instar myrrheis:</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The right part of the page is cut off, so lines end abruptly; the running head is cut at its right end. The line "Prata tundens florea." carries a marginal mark at the left edge. Doubtful readings: "gregex" may be "grex"; "Qua meus gregex" is as printed. Lower part of the page; the upper part is cut off. Some letters in the verse are doubtful (e.g. "vnguin^a" at line end, possibly "vnguina"), and the ligature-like mark after "vnguin" is uncertain.</notes>
</page>
